{
  "goal": "Add a --json flag to the taskly list command, following the council outcome (option 1). The default text output stays unchanged. With --json, stdout contains only a JSON array of {id, title, done}. The format lives in a separate toJSON helper, and list() stays text-only. The README documents both modes. The scripting consumer is unverified, but the council recommended proceeding. The plan uses 2 small items, one for the code and one for the docs.",
  "items": [
    {
      "id": "list-json-flag",
      "title": "Add --json output mode to list",
      "spec": "Edit src/list.js only. Keep tasks, formatText and list(all) behaviour unchanged; list still returns the text form. Add next to list: function toJSON(all) { return JSON.stringify(all.map(({ id, title, done }) => ({ id, title, done })), null, 2); }. Export it: module.exports = { list, formatText, toJSON }. Replace the main guard on line 9 with: if (require.main === module) console.log(process.argv.includes('--json') ? toJSON(tasks) : list(tasks)); In JSON mode stdout must contain only the array (plus console.log's trailing newline). Do not write anything else to stdout. Do not change package.json: bin points directly at src/list.js, so argv is [node, script, 'list', '--json'] and includes('--json') is the check. No new dependencies. Add no comments.",
      "owns": ["src/list.js"],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "seatId": null,
      "checks": [
        { "name": "default output runs", "cmd": "node src/list.js" },
        { "name": "json output is a 3-item array", "cmd": "node -e \"const o=require('child_process').execFileSync(process.execPath,['src/list.js','--json']).toString();const a=JSON.parse(o);if(!Array.isArray(a)||a.length!==3)process.exit(1)\"" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "readme-json-docs",
      "title": "Document list --json in README",
      "spec": "Edit README.md only. Keep the existing line 5 (taskly list) as the text-mode entry, with its wording and column alignment. Add a second usage line in the same indented block: taskly list --json, described as printing every task as a JSON array of {id, title, done}. State that the default output is unchanged and that --json writes only the array to stdout, so it can be piped. Keep the edit short. Do not edit other files.",
      "owns": ["README.md"],
      "dependsOn": [],
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "seatId": null,
      "checks": [
        { "name": "readme mentions --json", "cmd": "node -e \"if(!require('fs').readFileSync('README.md','utf8').includes('--json'))process.exit(1)\"" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
